before:
```typescript
type DoorState = "open" | "closed";
let state: DoorState = "closed";
state = "open";
console.log(state);
```

This prints open. The binding may change between the two allowed strings. The alias DoorState is erased when JavaScript is emitted; the runtime value is still an ordinary string.

after:
This variable can switch between the two allowed states.
```typescript
type DoorState = "open" | "closed";
let state: DoorState = "closed";
state = "open";
console.log(state);
```
The output is open.
